  "worked_solution": "First, we must find the elements of the set $A.$ Substituting the values $n\\in {1,2,3}$ into the formula $2{n}^{2},$ we get the following elements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=1 & \\,\u21d2\\,2\\cdot {1}^{2}=2 \\\\ n=2 & \\,\u21d2\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2}=8 \\\\ n=3 & \\,\u21d2\\,2\\cdot {3}^{2}=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA={2,8,18}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A\u2288B$ is false. Every element in the set $A$ is an element of the set $B.$\n\n- $\u2205\u2286B$ is true. The null set $\u2205={}$ is a subset of *every* set.\n\n- $B\u2286A$ is false. For example, $0\\in B$ but $0\\notin A.$\n\n- $A\u2287B$ is equivalent to $B\u2286A,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
